<section class="shell band">
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h2>If you are new</h2>
      <p>The portal is for people who have already started. A first contact goes through the
      <a href="/contact/">consult</a> instead: fifteen minutes, free, and the point of it is to
      work out whether this is the right fit before anyone books anything.</p>
      <p>After the consult you get a portal invitation, the forms, and a first appointment. That
      order matters, because the paperwork asks questions that only make sense once you know who
      you are working with.</p>
      <h3>Seeing an associate?</h3>
      <p>Each of the <a href="/therapy/associates/">LPC Associates</a> runs their own
      scheduling, billing and paperwork, so book and pay with them directly using the contact
      route on their card. Fees range from $100 to $165 a session with limited sliding-scale
      places.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Supervision and consultation</h3>
      <p>LPC supervision and EMDR consultation are not booked through the client portal.
      Supervision starts with an application, and consultation is scheduled directly.</p>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li><a href="/for-therapists/lpc-supervision/">LPC supervision</a>, $425 a month, by
        application</li>
        <li><a href="/for-therapists/emdr-consultation/">EMDR consultation</a>, $185 an hour,
        scheduled as needed</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>A note on security</h3>
      <p>No part of reemglascolpc.com asks for card numbers, insurance details or anything
      clinical. If a page claiming to be this practice does, it is not this practice. Payment
      happens inside the portal, on the portal's own domain.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions about booking and payment</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>How do I book a therapy session?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Existing clients book through the client portal. If you have not started yet, request a
      free 15-minute consult first; the portal invitation follows once you decide to go ahead.
      Clients of the practice's associates book directly with their associate.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How do I pay for a session?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>By major credit card inside the client portal. Blue Cross Blue Shield is accepted and
      billed through insurance; sessions under any other plan are self-pay at $240 for 50
      minutes. In-person walk therapy is paid in advance.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What happens if I cancel?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Telehealth appointments canceled at least 24 hours ahead cost nothing. Inside 24 hours
      an $85 fee may apply. Walk therapy is paid in advance and is not refunded for
      cancellations inside 48 hours.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do I have to be in Texas for a telehealth session?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Yes. A Texas license allows a counselor to treat clients located in Texas, so both you
      and your therapist have to be physically in the state at the time of the session. Tell your
      therapist in advance if you are traveling, so the appointment can be moved rather than
      canceled.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Can I use the portal to reach my therapist between sessions?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>For scheduling and admin, yes. It is not a crisis channel and messages are not monitored
      around the clock. If you are in crisis, call or text 988, or 911 if you are in immediate
      danger.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  {% include "partials/crisis-note.njk" %}
</section>

